atlas external

architecture obsidian-vault-binding
  canonical_name ObsidianVaultBinding
  family external
  domain External / Personal knowledge vaults
  layer external
  semantic_question Which Obsidian vault folders on this device belong to which account, how are they read, written and synced (desktop CLI, Obsidian Headless or the files themselves), and when is headless sync refused?
  purpose Binds a local Obsidian vault folder to exactly one account and gives every flow one contract over it. Reads (search, tasks, backlinks, links, unresolved, tags, properties, read) go through the running desktop app's CLI when the binding asks for it and the app is up, otherwise through native readers over the files. Writes (create, append, prepend, daily-append, task) go the same way, natively as atomic same-folder writes. Obsidian Headless (ob) runs per account under its own HOME so each account has its own Obsidian login; sync-setup, sync-config, sync-once and a supervised continuous sync (child process with pidfile, or a launchd agent) are refused wherever desktop Sync is on for the vault, as Obsidian requires. Content-addressed snapshots record every file's sha256, size and mtime incrementally and diff against each other for local sync.
  maturity implemented
  consumes AccountSubject
  owns ObsidianVaultBinding
  publishes ObsidianNoteRef
  publishes ObsidianTaskRef
  publishes ObsidianGuardDecision
  publishes ObsidianSyncRun
  publishes ObsidianSnapshot
  node_types ObsidianVaultBinding
  node_types ObsidianNoteRef
  node_types ObsidianTaskRef
  node_types ObsidianGuardDecision
  node_types ObsidianSyncRun
  node_types ObsidianReceipt
  node_types ObsidianSnapshot
  state_types bound
  state_types sync-configured
  state_types syncing
  internal_calculus path containment: relative slash paths, no dot or dot-dot or dot-led component, never the config folder in any case; reads resolve inside the real root, writes lstat every parent and refuse a symlink
  internal_calculus Obsidian link resolution: markdown links relative to the note, wikilinks with a folder by path suffix, bare names by case-insensitive filename preferring the note's folder then the shortest path
  internal_calculus headless guard: transport, desktop Sync core plugin (object or array form), a running app's sync:status, another account's or an unscoped ob setup for the same real folder
  internal_calculus incremental snapshot: reuse a file's recorded sha256 when size and mtime match, hash otherwise; manifest digest is sha256 over path, sha256 and size lines in byte order
  command bonfyre-obsidian
  source_path cmd/BonfyreObsidian/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreObsidian/src/vault.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreObsidian/src/drive.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreObsidian/src/obsidian.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreObsidian/Makefile
  source_path cmd/BonfyreObsidian/README.md
  source_path schemas/control/obsidian.yaff
  source_path schemas/control/obsidian.cue
  witness cmd/BonfyreObsidian/tests/obsidian_test.sh (149 checks, 2026-10-31, throwaway vaults): one folder per account and no nesting; another account's vault refused exactly as an absent one; a symlink out of the allowed roots refused at bind; eight escaping or hidden note paths refused on read and four on write, nothing written through a linked folder; search, tasks (fenced task excluded, numbered and nested included), backlinks (wikilink, lower-case and markdown), outgoing links, unresolved, tags (frontmatter and body, none from code or digits) and properties match a hand-built fixture; create, overwrite, append from stdin, prepend after frontmatter, daily-append and task toggle write the expected bytes and receipt them without content; snapshots reuse every hash when nothing changed, rehash only the two touched files and diff to one added, one removed, one changed; another account cannot diff them
  witness cmd/BonfyreObsidian/tests/obsidian_test.sh with recording shims for ob, obsidian and launchctl (argv and environment only): the guard refuses a desktop-Sync vault before ob is run, refuses a folder another account's or an unscoped ob setup syncs, and allows a clean one; ob runs under the account's own HOME with no password, email or MFA flag; OBSIDIAN_AUTH_TOKEN reaches ob only for the account BONFYRE_OBSIDIAN_TOKEN_ACCOUNT names and never the store, logs or output; continuous sync starts once, is seen again, blocks unbind, stops, and a reused pid is called stale and not signalled; a launchd plist names ob, the folder and the account HOME, lints, and bootstrap and bootout carry the right argv; the CLI is never called while the app is down, its JSON is passed through when up, a failing CLI falls back to native, writes escape newlines, and a running app reporting Sync refuses headless sync
  witness cmd/BonfyreObsidian/tests/real_readonly_test.sh against /Users/nickgonzales/Documents/AurekaiV2 (2026-10-31, 15 checks): doctor found Obsidian 1.12.7 running, its CLI not registered, ob 0.0.14 on Node 26.13.0 and no login; native search found the same 7 lines grep finds, one unresolved link ([[create a link]]), no tasks; the guard refused headless sync because the vault's Sync core plugin is on; every file's size, mtime and sha256 were identical before and after
  invariant a real folder is bound at most once across all accounts and never inside or around another bound folder; local_path is the real path after symlinks and lies inside a configured root (BONFYRE_OBSIDIAN_ROOTS)
  invariant every verb but doctor requires --account; a vault another account bound answers exactly as one nobody bound
  invariant Obsidian's settings folder is never read or written through a note verb; a write follows no symlink and lands by write, fsync, then rename (or link when the note must not yet exist)
  invariant headless sync is refused where the desktop Sync core plugin is on for the vault, where a running app reports Sync, or where another account's or an unscoped Obsidian Headless setup already syncs the folder
  invariant the desktop CLI is called only when the app is already running (or BONFYRE_OBSIDIAN_CLI_LAUNCH=1), because the CLI starts the app otherwise
  invariant ob runs per account under HOME=<state>/accounts/<account>/home; no password, email or MFA code is ever placed on argv; OBSIDIAN_AUTH_TOKEN is removed from ob's environment except for the one named account
  invariant a receipt holds paths, digests, codes and reasons, never note content or a credential
  forbidden_inference a binding -> the account owns, pays for or may share the remote Obsidian vault
  forbidden_inference headless sync configured -> desktop Sync is off for that vault on every device; the guard reads this device only
  forbidden_inference guard allow -> the remote vault is safe to overwrite; mirror-remote and pull-only still discard local edits by design
  forbidden_inference CLI reachable -> the app's state is the vault on disk; unsaved editor text and an unrescanned index differ from the files
  forbidden_inference a native answer -> the app's answer; link resolution, tags and properties follow Obsidian's rules on the files, not its live index or plugins
  forbidden_inference token_file_present -> a valid login or a Sync subscription; only the file's presence is read
  forbidden_inference equal size and mtime -> equal bytes; a writer that restores mtime is missed until a fresh snapshot without history
  forbidden_inference an account name on a call -> that the caller authenticated as it; the calling boundary authenticates
  known_gap the desktop CLI is not registered on this Mac, so no real CLI call has been made; CLI argv and the shapes passed through are witnessed only against a recording shim, and the CLI's own JSON shapes are passed through unnormalized
  known_gap no Obsidian login exists for any account here and no real Headless Sync has run; ob's argv, HOME and token handling are witnessed against a shim, not Obsidian's servers
  known_gap the Obsidian Headless token is held in ob's own auth_token file under the account HOME, not sealed by CredentialBoundary, which has no path that hands a raw value to a child process
  known_gap the organ trusts --account from its caller; no web route, MCP tool or flow calls it yet, so nothing authenticates the account in front of it
  known_gap headless Publish (publish-*) is not exposed; Obsidian Bases (base:query) and outline are reachable only through the CLI, with no native reader
  known_gap the binary stays in cmd/BonfyreObsidian; it is not installed to ~/.bonfyre/bin while the install budget is spent

interaction credential-accounts-name-obsidian-accounts
  source credential-boundary
  destination obsidian-vault-binding
  relation same_account_grammar
  preserves an account is one lowercase name of letters, digits and - _ . @ + up to 128, so one account names its credentials and its vaults alike
  drops sealed values; no credential moves from the boundary to Obsidian Headless, whose token stays in ob's own file under the account HOME
  forbidden_inference a CredentialBoundary account having a sealed value -> an Obsidian login for that account
  forbidden_inference an Obsidian binding under an account -> a credential stored for it
  invalidates_on either owner changing its account alphabet
  witness cmd/BonfyreObsidian/tests/obsidian_test.sh
  binding cmd/BonfyreObsidian/src/main.c
  binding cmd/BonfyreCredentials/src/main.c

interaction obsidian-command-realizes-vault-binding
  source cmd-obsidian
  destination obsidian-vault-binding
  relation realizes
  preserves every verb, JSON shape and exit code in cmd/BonfyreObsidian/README.md
  drops authentication of the caller, which belongs to the boundary in front of the command
  forbidden_inference the command answering -> the caller may act for the account it named
  invalidates_on a verb, shape or exit code changing in README.md
  witness cmd/BonfyreObsidian/tests/obsidian_test.sh
  binding cmd/BonfyreObsidian/src/main.c
